(Characterizing Rehabilitation Intensity in Stroke Recovery: A Cross-Site Canadian Practice) Tj
T*
(Survey) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Purpose: Current clinical guidelines recommend high-intensity stepping activities and) Tj
T*
(cardiovascular exercise during inpatient stroke rehabilitation, yet implementation and) Tj
T*
(adherence to these targets remain unclear. This descriptive protocol aims to characterize) Tj
T*
(rehabilitation intensity during typical physical therapy sessions across multiple Canadian) Tj
T*
(rehabilitation facilities. Methods: We will conduct a cross-sectional assessment of) Tj
T*
(rehabilitation sessions at a sample of Canadian inpatient stroke rehabilitation units.) Tj
T*
(Inclusion criteria are medically stable stroke survivors admitted for inpatient) Tj
T*
(rehabilitation, minimum functional capacity to ambulate with assistance of one person.) Tj
T*
(Participants will be assessed during one rehabilitation session using objective devices:) Tj
T*
(wrist-worn monitors will quantify aerobic exercise time \(defined as exercise exceeding 40%) Tj
T*
(heart rate reserve\), and ankle-worn step counters will record step numbers. We will) Tj
T*
(describe the distribution of aerobic minutes and step counts, their correlation with) Tj
T*
(participant characteristics, and documentation of guideline-adherent exercise intensities.) Tj
T*
(Data will be analyzed using descriptive statistics and correlation methods. This) Tj
T*
(observational study will provide baseline data on current rehabilitation practice) Tj
T*
(patterns.) Tj
